# Entity Patterns

This guide outlines advanced patterns and best practices for writing entities in the `./demo` directory.

## Base Types and Inheritance
- Use base types when multiple variants share common properties
- Extend base types using intersection types for variants
- Name variants consistently with their base type
- Example:
  ```typescript
  // Base type with common properties
  type BaseTodo = {
    id: ID["TODO"];
    name: string;
    done: boolean;
  };

  // Variants extending base type
  type ToggleTodo = BaseTodo & {
    type: TODO_TYPE["TOGGLE"];
  };

  type ReportTodo = BaseTodo & {
    type: TODO_TYPE["REPORT"];
    report: RichTextContent;
    minReportLength: number;
  };
  ```

## Discriminated Unions
- Use enum types as discriminator fields
- Place discriminator field first in each variant
- Keep variant-specific fields after the discriminator
- Example:
  ```typescript
  type PaneContent =
    | {
        type: PANE_CONTENT_TYPE["MEMO"];  // discriminator field
        memoId: ID["MEMO"];
      }
    | {
        type: PANE_CONTENT_TYPE["TODO_LIST"];  // discriminator field
        todoListId: ID["TODO_LIST"];
      };
  ```

## Property Modifiers
- Use `readonly` modifier to indicate that a property represents an immutable business concept
- This is for documentation purposes only, as entities are typically immutable in React applications
- Use optional properties (`?`) sparingly and document why they're optional
- Example:
  ```typescript
  type Todo = {
    readonly id: ID["TODO"];  // Immutable business concept
    readonly createdAt: Timestamp;  // Immutable business concept
    name: string; // Mutable content
    description?: string;  // Optional with reason
  };
  ```

## Field Ordering
- Place primary identifier at the very top of the type definition.
- Place readonly fields at the top of the type definition
- Example:
  ```typescript
  type Memo = {
    readonly id: ID["MEMO"];        // 
    readonly createdAt: Timestamp;  // Immutable fields first
    content: RichTextContent;       // Mutable fields next
    modifiedAt?: Timestamp;         
  };
  ```

